// Faces to triangles.
//
// Face f owns loops [off[f], off[f+1]) and each loop names a vertex through
// `.corner_vert`. A face of n corners becomes n-2 triangles fanned from its first
// corner, which is correct for any convex face and is what Blender's own
// triangulation does for the common quad.
//
// The winding is preserved: Blender's faces are counter-clockwise seen from
// outside, and a fan keeps that, so back-face culling works on the result
// without anything here knowing which way the renderer looks.

bl_faces(int p, int si) {
  int cv = bl_afind(p, si, ".corner_vert");
  int po = bl_faces_po(p, si);
  int ret_i = bl_faces_tris(cv, po, p, si);
} return int ret_i;
